*mut T`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Size of `#[repr(C)]` items"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The `C` representation for items has a defined layout. With this layout,"},{"DocComment":" the size of items is also stable as long as all fields have a stable size."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ## Size of Structs"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" For `struct`s, the size is determined by the following algorithm."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" For each field in the struct ordered by declaration order:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" 1. Add the size of the field."},{"DocComment":" 2. Round up the current size to the nearest multiple of the next field's [alignment]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Finally, round the size of the struct to the nearest multiple of its [alignment]."},{"DocComment":" The alignment of the struct is usually the largest alignment of all its"},{"DocComment":" fields; this can be changed with the use of `repr(align(N))`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Unlike `C`, zero sized structs are not rounded up to one byte in size."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ## Size of Enums"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Enums that carry no data other than the discriminant have the same size as C enums"},{"DocComment":" on the platform they are compiled for."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ## Size of Unions"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The size of a union is the size of its largest field."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Unlike `C`, zero sized unions are not rounded up to one byte in size."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" // Some primitives"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(4, size_of::<i32>());"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(8, size_of::<f64>());"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(0, size_of::<()>());"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" // Some arrays"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(8, size_of::<[i32; 2]>());"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(12, size_of::<[i32; 3]>());"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(0, size_of::<[i32; 0]>());"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" // Pointer size equality"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(size_of::<&i32>(), size_of::<*const i32>());"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(size_of::<&i32>(), size_of::<Box<i32>>());"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(size_of::<&i32>(), size_of::<Option<&i32>>());"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(size_of::<Box<i32>>(), size_of::<Option<Box<i32>>>());"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Using `#[repr(C)]`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" #[repr(C)]"},{"DocComment":" struct FieldStruct {"},{"DocComment":"     first: u8,"},{"DocComment":"     second: u16,"},{"DocComment":"     third: u8"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" // The size of the first field is 1, so add 1 to the size. Size is 1."},{"DocComment":" // The alignment of the second field is 2, so add 1 to the size for padding. Size is 2."},{"DocComment":" // The size of the second field is 2, so add 2 to the size. Size is 4."},{"DocComment":" // The alignment of the third field is 1, so add 0 to the size for padding. Size is 4."},{"DocComment":" // The size of the third field is 1, so add 1 to the size. Size is 5."},{"DocComment":" // Finally, the alignment of the struct is 2 (because the largest alignment amongst its"},{"DocComment":" // fields is 2), so add 1 to the size for padding. Size is 6."},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(6, size_of::<FieldStruct>());"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" #[repr(C)]"},{"DocComment":" struct TupleStruct(u8, u16, u8);"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" // Tuple structs follow the same rules."},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(6, size_of::<TupleStruct>());"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" // Note that reordering the fields can lower the size. We can remove both padding bytes"},{"DocComment":" // by putting `third` before `second`."},{"DocComment":" #[repr(C)]"},{"DocComment":" struct FieldStructOptimized {"},{"DocComment":"     first: u8,"},{"DocComment":"     third: u8,"},{"DocComment":"     second: u16"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(4, size_of::<FieldStructOptimized>());"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" // Union size is the size of the largest field."},{"DocComment":" #[repr(C)]"},{"DocComment":" union ExampleUnion {"},{"DocComment":"     smaller: u8,"},{"DocComment":"     larger: u16"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(2, size_of::<ExampleUnion>());"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [alignment]: align_of"},{"DocComment":" [`*const T`]: primitive@pointer"},{"DocComment":" [`Box<T>`]: ../../std/boxed/struct.Box.html"},{"DocComment":" [`Option<&T>`]: crate::option::Option"},{"DocComment":""}],"inline":"Always","rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"started_from":false,"is_extern":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item":"mem_size_of","has_errors":false},"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"signature":{"is_unsafe":false,"abi":"Rust","is_variadic":false,"inputs":[],"output":{"Deduplicated":0}},"src":"Normal","body":"Opaque"},{"def_id":57,"item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["mem",0]},{"Ident":["size_of",0]},{"Instantiated":{"params":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"skip_binder":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Deduplicated":11}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"kind":"Other"}}],"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":9,"beg":{"line":375,"col":0},"end":{"line":375,"col":34}},"generated_from_span":null}},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Returns the size of a type in bytes."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" More specifically, this is the offset in bytes between successive elements"},{"DocComment":" in an array with tha