 2. Round up the current size to the nearest multiple of the next field's [alignment]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Finally, round the size of the struct to the nearest multiple of its [alignment]."},{"DocComment":" The alignment of the struct is usually the largest alignment of all its"},{"DocComment":" fields; this can be changed with the use of `repr(align(N))`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Unlike `C`, zero sized structs are not rounded up to one byte in size."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ## Size of Enums"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Enums that carry no data other than the discriminant have the same size as C enums"},{"DocComment":" on the platform they are compiled for."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ## Size of Unions"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The size of a union is the size of its largest field."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Unlike `C`, zero sized unions are not rounded up to one byte in size."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" // Some primitives"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(4, size_of::<i32>());"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(8, size_of::<f64>());"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(0, size_of::<()>());"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" // Some arrays"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(8, size_of::<[i32; 2]>());"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(12, size_of::<[i32; 3]>());"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(0, size_of::<[i32; 0]>());"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" // Pointer size equality"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(size_of::<&i32>(), size_of::<*const i32>());"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(size_of::<&i32>(), size_of::<Box<i32>>());"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(size_of::<&i32>(), size_of::<Option<&i32>>());"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(size_of::<Box<i32>>(), size_of::<Option<Box<i32>>>());"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Using `#[repr(C)]`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" #[repr(C)]"},{"DocComm